lved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "stdout", "first_after_build": true, "first_side": "without", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "opencode", "harness_version": "0.0.0--202610170413 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/opencode-src/bin/6b4d617df080cef71cd8f4b041601cf47ce0edf3/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: bash]\nAll bugs are clear. Applying fixes:\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: edit]\nAll 16 tests pass now. Before the fix the run showed 15 tests, because `tests/test_search.py` couldn't be imported at all; its 2 tests run now. I didn't change any tests.\n\n**The three reads you asked for:**\n- **(a)** Reading `catalog/` gave a list of 8 files: `__init__.py`, `books.py`, `factory.py`, `fees.py`, `inventory.py`, `members.py`, `search.py`, `text.py`.\n- **(b)** Offset 0, limit 5 returned lines 1\u20135.\n- **(c)** Offset 3, limit 5 returned lines 4\u20138.\n\nSo `offset` counts from 0: it's the number of lines skipped, and offset 3 starts at line 4.\n\n**Fixes:**\n1. `catalog/books.py:22`: `parse_book` left the year as a string, so it's now converted with `int(year)`. This also fixed `age()`, which was failing because it subtracted a string from a number.\n2. `catalog/factory.py`: added the missing `Emma` book, so the sample has the three titles its docstring lists.\n3. `catalog/fees.py:14`: the fee was days plus the daily rate; it's now days times the rate (`days_late * DAILY_FEE`).\n4. `catalog/inventory.py`: `recent(n)` returned one event too many. It now returns the last `n` (`self._history[-n:]`). I also made `n <= 0` return an empty list, because `[-0:]` would otherwise return the whole history. No test needs that guard; it just prevents a wrong result.\n5. `catalog/members.py:4`: changed `MAX_BORROWED` from 3 to 5, which matches the comment above it and the tests.\n6. `catalog/search.py:3`: the import pointed at a module that doesn't exist (`catalog.nonexistent`). It now imports `normalize` from `catalog.text`.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": ["param:temperature"], "params_stripped_requests": 1, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 8, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 50624, "requests_cache_write": 61291, "requests_cost_usd": 0.3756638, "requests_count": 6, "requests_input_uncached": 16, "requests_output": 2951, "reread": true, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "opencode:trig-read-edge:claude-opus-5-5:trial1", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 9, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-18T06:19:42.167295+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 32.223, "t_checker_s": 0.176, "t_env_setup_s": 0.002, "task": "trig-read-edge", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "vendor_split", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 2967, "tokens_cache_read": 50624, "tokens_cache_write": 61291, "tokens_fresh": 2949, "tokens_input_uncached": 16, "tokens_main_cache_read": 49592, "tokens_main_cache_write": 61291, "tokens_main_calls": 5, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 12, "tokens_main_output": 2937, "tokens_output": 2951, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 50624, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": 61291, "tokens_proxy_calls": 6, "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": 16, "tokens_proxy_output": 2951, "tokens_